parameters.text:
=Ideal customer profile:
{{ $json.icp }}
Country: {{ $json.country }}

Write 5 Google queries that surface LinkedIn company pages matching this profile. Each query must contain the operator site:linkedin.com/company. Vary the angle across queries: industry wording, product category, the job titles such a company would be hiring, and the technology it would run. Return the query string only - no explanation inside the query.

parameters.jsCode:
// Keep only real LinkedIn company pages, one row per company.
const seen = new Set();
const out = [];
const errors = [];

for (const item of $input.all()) {
  let payload = item.json.body ?? item.json;
  if (typeof payload === 'string') {
    try { payload = JSON.parse(payload); } catch { continue; }
  }
  // Bright Data answers 200 with an error body, so a bad request looks
  // like an empty SERP unless we read it.
  if (payload && payload.error) {
    const detail = Array.isArray(payload.details)
      ? payload.details.map((d) => d.message).join('; ')
      : '';
    errors.push(payload.error + (detail ? ': ' + detail : ''));
    continue;
  }
  for (const r of (payload.organic ?? [])) {
    const link = r.link || r.url;
    if (!link) continue;
    // /company/<slug> only - skip /jobs, /posts, /showcase and locale variants
    const m = link.match(/linkedin\.com\/company\/([a-z0-9\-_.%]+)/i);
    if (!m) continue;
    const slug = m[1].toLowerCase();
    if (seen.has(slug)) continue;
    seen.add(slug);
    out.push({ json: {
      slug,
      linkedin_url: `https://www.linkedin.com/company/${slug}`,
      serp_title: r.title ?? '',
      serp_snippet: r.description ?? '',
    }});
  }
}

if (out.length === 0 && errors.length) {
  throw new Error(`Bright Data rejected the SERP request: ${errors[0]}`);
}

if (out.length === 0) {
  throw new Error('No LinkedIn company pages found. Check that serp_zone in Search Config matches a zone in your Bright Data account, and that the ICP is specific enough to search for.');
}

return out;

// The scraper returns one array of company objects. Flatten to n8n items and
// keep only the fields the scorer needs - a full LinkedIn record is mostly noise.
// Bright Data may hand back one item per company (n8n split the array) or a
// single item holding the whole array. Read every input item, or we keep only
// the first company and silently drop the rest.
const rows = [];

for (const item of $input.all()) {
  let payload = item.json.body ?? item.json;
  if (typeof payload === 'string') {
    try { payload = JSON.parse(payload); } catch { continue; }
  }
  if (payload && payload.snapshot_id && !Array.isArray(payload)) {
    throw new Error(`Bright Data returned snapshot_id ${payload.snapshot_id} instead of rows, which means the sync request passed its 1-minute limit. Lower "How many companies", or switch this node to the async endpoint /datasets/v3/trigger and poll /datasets/v3/progress.`);
  }
  if (Array.isArray(payload)) rows.push(...payload);
  else if (payload) rows.push(payload);
}

const out = [];

for (const c of rows) {
  if (!c || (!c.name && !c.company_name)) continue;
  out.push({ json: {
    name: c.name ?? c.company_name ?? '',
    linkedin_url: c.url ?? c.input?.url ?? '',
    website: c.website ?? '',
    industry: c.industries ?? c.industry ?? '',
    employees: c.employees_in_linkedin ?? c.company_size ?? null,
    headquarters: c.headquarters ?? c.locations?.[0] ?? '',
    founded: c.founded ?? null,
    specialties: Array.isArray(c.specialties) ? c.specialties.join(', ') : (c.specialties ?? ''),
    about: (c.about ?? c.description ?? '').slice(0, 1500),
    followers: c.followers ?? null,
  }});
}

if (out.length === 0) {
  throw new Error('The scraper returned no usable company records. The URLs may be private or region-blocked pages.');
}

return out;

parameters.text:
=IDEAL CUSTOMER PROFILE:
{{ $('Set Search Parameters').first().json.icp }}

COMPANY:
Name: {{ $json.name }}
Industry: {{ $json.industry }}
Employees: {{ $json.employees }}
HQ: {{ $json.headquarters }}
Founded: {{ $json.founded }}
Specialties: {{ $json.specialties }}
About: {{ $json.about }}

Score 0-100 for fit against the profile. Judge only the company facts above - you have not been told what search found this company, and you should not assume it matches just because it surfaced.

Quote the specific fact behind the score. If a criterion in the profile cannot be checked from these fields, list it under missing rather than assuming it passes.

parameters.jsCode:
// Pair each score back to its company. informationExtractor preserves order.
const companies = $('Flatten Company Records').all();
const cfg = $('Set Search Parameters').first().json;

return $input.all().map((item, i) => {
  const c = companies[i]?.json ?? {};
  const s = item.json.output ?? {};
  const score = Number(s.score ?? 0);
  return { json: {
    run_id: cfg.run_id,
    scored_at: $now.toISO(),
    name: c.name,
    website: c.website,
    linkedin_url: c.linkedin_url,
    industry: c.industry,
    employees: c.employees,
    headquarters: c.headquarters,
    score,
    tier: s.tier ?? '',
    evidence: s.evidence ?? '',
    missing: Array.isArray(s.missing) ? s.missing.join('; ') : (s.missing ?? ''),
    objection: s.objection ?? '',
    qualified: score >= Number(cfg.min_score),
  }};
});
